# NOTE: pnpm 11 no longer reads install-tuning settings from .npmrc (verified
# 2026-08-01 — `pnpm config get` returned undefined for every key set here). The
# build-resilience settings that used to live here (networkConcurrency, fetchRetries,
# verifyStoreIntegrity, etc. — to survive npm-registry 429s during cold Docker builds)
# now live in pnpm-workspace.yaml, which is where pnpm 11 actually reads them. Keep
# registry-auth / npm-compatible entries here if ever needed; put pnpm settings there.

# Kept from feat/deployment. This one is NOT install tuning — it disables pnpm 11's
# supply-chain policy check, the phase that makes ~2000 registry metadata requests on a
# cold build and got us rate-limited (ERR_PNPM_FETCH_429) twice. It is left here rather
# than dropped because it is harmless if unread, and the note above only established
# that *install-tuning* keys are ignored — it was never verified for this key.
#
# It is also not load-bearing today: the long, patient retry settings in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml are what actually carried the 2026-08-08 production build through
# that same phase without a 429. Treat this as belt-and-braces, not the fix.
supply-chain-policy=false
